This skill's discussion loop and red-team pass are structured on prior work by
others. No prose was copied; what is borrowed is method. Short functional field
labels ("fails if", "kill criterion") are reused as terms of art.

- The widening move (one question at a time, multiple-choice where the options
  are discrete, several approaches with trade-offs before converging) follows
  the "brainstorming" skill from obra/superpowers,
  https://github.com/obra/superpowers
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Jesse Vincent.

- The assumption-attack structure (fails-if / cheapest evidence / kill criterion,
  ranked by damage against cost to check) and the "neither manufacture doubt nor
  rubber-stamp" discipline follow the "strategy-red-team" skill from
  phuryn/pm-skills, https://github.com/phuryn/pm-skills
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Pawel Huryn.

  Both license texts were read from the upstream repositories on 2026-07-28.
  Because no substantial portion of either work is reproduced here, the MIT
  attribution condition is not triggered; the credit above is given anyway.

- The context-gathering entry and the fresh-context verification step are adapted
  from the "doc-coauthoring" example skill published by Anthropic. The copy this
  was read from shipped without a license file, unlike its sibling example
  skills (Apache-2.0), so its terms are unconfirmed. Only the method is used —
  ask before drafting, then test the artifact against a reader with no context.
  If you intend to redistribute this skill, confirm that skill's terms first.

